# TypeScript Conventions

- Keep TypeScript guidance within the MVP architecture already described in the product spec.
- Use TypeScript for application, worker, package, and tooling code.
- Prefer shared types, validators, and schemas from owning packages over duplicating JSON shape assumptions.
- Keep framework-specific code inside its owning app: Next.js concerns in `apps/web`, worker pipeline concerns in `apps/worker`.
- Put reusable model, curriculum, activity, database, and eval logic in the matching package under `packages/*`.
- Avoid adding abstractions until they remove real duplication or match an established local pattern.
- When adding scripts or tooling, wire them so they work from the repository root with pnpm workspaces.
